.TH MX-TOOLS 1 "2026-07-20" "MX Linux" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
mx-tools \- open MX Linux configuration tools
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mx-tools
.RI [ option ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mx-tools
is a graphical launcher for configuration and maintenance tools provided by MX Linux. Select a tool from the application window to open it.
.SH OPTIONS
Each of the following options can be used on its own without a graphical session.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print command-line help and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-help-all
Print help including Qt-specific options and exit.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Print the application version and exit.
.SH RENDERING
On X11, MX Tools uses Qt Quick's software renderer by default so the dashboard
can open even when OpenGL initialization fails. Tools launched from MX Tools
are not affected. To request OpenGL, run
.PP
.EX
QSG_RHI_BACKEND=opengl mx-tools
.EE
.PP
To request software rendering explicitly on any platform, run
.PP
.EX
QT_QUICK_BACKEND=software mx-tools
.EE
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/share/doc/mx-tools
Installed license, help, and changelog documentation.
.SH AUTHOR
MX Linux contributors.
